# Documented, scoped suppressions for the data-platform images.
#
# Every entry needs a reason and a re-check date. A .trivyignore without those is
# indistinguishable from turning the scanner off, and the whole value of a gate is
# that suppressing something is a deliberate, reviewable act.
#
# Both scanned images now delete pip before the scan runs, so nothing pip VENDORS
# is reachable here. The entries that covered pip's bundled msgpack and setuptools
# are gone rather than carried: those copies no longer exist in the image, and a
# suppression keyed on a CVE id would also hide that CVE if it came back in a real
# dependency.
#
# What remains is a package this repo actually installs — see its entry below.

# sqlparse — three HIGH advisories, all fixed in 0.6.0, which cannot be installed:
#
#   dbt-core 1.12.0 depends on sqlparse<0.6.0 and >=0.5.5
#
# Verified by attempting it: pinning sqlparse>=0.6.0 fails the image build with
# ResolutionImpossible. The upgrade is therefore blocked upstream, not skipped.
#
# Exposure: sqlparse is used by dbt to parse THIS REPOSITORY'S OWN model SQL at
# build time. It never parses user input and never runs at serving time — the
# runtime image contains neither dbt nor sqlparse. The advisories concern parsing
# hostile SQL, which is not a path that exists here.
#
# Re-check: 2026-11-18, or when dbt-core relaxes its sqlparse pin.
CVE-2026-54284
CVE-2026-59893
CVE-2026-71491
